            <ArticleTitle>Pharmacological mechanisms underlying the association of antipsychotics with metabolic disorders.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>12-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.12865/CHSJ.40.01.02</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity and metabolic syndrome in association with an increased risk of cardiovascular disease and type II diabetes are significant problems that contribute to lower life expectancy of patients with schizophrenia. Understanding the pharmacological mechanisms of the current antipsychotic treatment is clearly the key to the improvement of pharmacotherapy, to avoid or to mitigate the metabolic adverse effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
